{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot perception and motion as separate automata, with all sensor outcomes as uncontrollable and all motion commands as controllable. The specification binds each perception outcome to a single safe, progress-oriented action, ensuring conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration. Oscillation is prevented by never enabling both rotations in the same state, and full_rotate is reserved for repeated recovery. All transitions are deterministic and total for uncontrollable events.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plant automata for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specification automaton enforces safe, progress-maximizing action selection per perception outcome, with conservative recovery and no oscillation."
